Version: [current]
Command: monochange step

Run built-in release workflow steps

[1m[97mUsage:[0m [93mmonochange step[0m [95m[OPTIONS][0m [95m<COMMAND>[0m

[1m[96mStep Commands:[0m
  [93mconfig[0m                    Render resolved monochange configuration and workspace metadata
  [93mvalidate[0m                  Validate configuration, changesets, and version groups
  [93mdiscover[0m                  Discover packages across supported ecosystems
  [93mdisplay-versions[0m          Show the next version for each release group and package without writing files
  [93mcreate-change-file[0m        Create a changeset file for one or more packages
  [93mprepare-release[0m           Plan version bumps, changelogs, and release artifacts
  [93mcommit-release[0m            Create a release commit that embeds the durable release record
  [93mverify-release-branch[0m     Verify a commit is reachable from a configured release branch
  [93mpublish-release[0m           Publish provider release objects from a prepared release artifact
  [93mplaceholder-publish[0m       Publish placeholder package versions for missing registry packages
  [93mpublish-packages[0m          Publish package versions from durable monochange release state
  [93mplan-publish-rate-limits[0m  Plan package-registry rate-limit windows for publish operations
  [93mopen-release-request[0m      Open or update the hosted release request from prepared release state
  [93mcomment-released-issues[0m   Comment on linked issues shipped in a prepared release
  [93maffected-packages[0m         Compute affected packages from a prepared release plan
  [93mdiagnose-changesets[0m       Inspect changeset provenance and review metadata
  [93mrelease-record[0m            Inspect the release record associated with a tag or commit
  [93mpublish-readiness[0m         Check package registry publishing readiness without publishing packages
  [93mtag-release[0m               Create and push release tags from a release record
  [93mretarget-release[0m          Repair a recent release by retargeting its release tags

[1m[96mOptions:[0m
  [93m-h[0m, [93m--help[0m
          Print help

[1m[96mGlobal Options:[0m
  [93m-q[0m, [93m--quiet[0m
          Suppress result, progress, and diagnostic output without changing execution

  [93m-v[0m, [93m--verbose[0m
          Show full result lists and logs, every step timing, and progress notes

      [93m--color[0m[95m [0m[95m<WHEN>[0m
          Control when output uses color; `auto` honors NO_COLOR, CLICOLOR, and CLICOLOR_FORCE

          [possible values: auto, always, never]

      [93m--progress-format[0m[95m [0m[95m<FORMAT>[0m
